WEBVTT

01:52.692 --> 01:54.228
Fenbren: Got you!

01:55.130 --> 01:58.837
Fenbren: Baran... falls!

02:03.046 --> 02:05.685
[roaring]

02:13.033 --> 02:14.970
Fenbren [thought]:
What... was that...

02:15.003 --> 02:17.341
Avan Strash?!

02:17.374 --> 02:19.746
That pathetic... kid...

02:20.515 --> 02:23.486
It's like I
was made to lose-

02:23.520 --> 02:28.329
To lose to everyone-
like I never stood a chance!

02:28.998 --> 02:33.373
Curse you! Curse you all!

02:36.279 --> 02:38.016
Dai [thought]:
It was all instinct.

02:38.049 --> 02:40.253
I've never felt
that before.

02:40.287 --> 02:43.761
It's like the sword's
will and mine were one.

02:43.794 --> 02:45.665
I forgot all about the seal.

02:45.699 --> 02:48.269
All I could think
about was saving...

02:51.308 --> 02:53.747
Baran: So. This is
your new weapon.

02:54.683 --> 02:55.918
Impressive.

03:00.327 --> 03:02.197
Baran: With both
of our blades,

03:02.231 --> 03:05.771
not even the legendary
Dark Citadel Gate will hold.

03:08.877 --> 03:10.380
Let's go, Dai.

03:10.414 --> 03:13.987
Put everything you've
got into this single strike.

03:14.021 --> 03:14.989
Dai: Okay.

03:26.646 --> 03:27.915
Dai: It worked!

03:37.234 --> 03:38.871
This is no earthquake...

03:43.681 --> 03:45.985
Mystvearn [thought]:
They've actually breached it.

03:46.018 --> 03:50.393
That gate was sealed by
the Dark King's own power.

03:55.938 --> 03:58.443
Send for another, Mystvearn.

03:58.476 --> 03:59.846
Mystvearn: Yes, sire.

04:01.016 --> 04:04.421
How very impressive.

04:04.455 --> 04:08.531
Dai: We did it. The entrance
to Vearn Palace is open.

04:08.564 --> 04:10.635
Baran: We were
bound to succeed.

04:10.668 --> 04:13.406
The combined might
of two Dragon Knights

04:13.439 --> 04:16.747
is a force this
world has never known.

04:16.781 --> 04:20.186
But breaching the gate
is only the beginning.

04:20.220 --> 04:21.990
Keep your guard up.

04:23.393 --> 04:27.568
Our real target is
the Dark King. Come now.

04:29.573 --> 04:32.912
This shaking...
it can only mean...

04:32.945 --> 04:36.452
Dai and Baran actually
breached the hidden gate.

04:43.032 --> 04:44.536
[realizing breath]

04:46.039 --> 04:47.642
Fenbren has fallen!

04:47.675 --> 04:48.610
Hym: No!

04:49.680 --> 04:50.548
Hym!

04:50.581 --> 04:52.418
Where are you going-
stop this!

04:52.451 --> 04:54.489
I'm going to
avenge my brother.

04:54.523 --> 04:55.758
Albinass: You will not.

04:57.562 --> 04:58.396
B-But...

04:58.430 --> 05:00.968
Have you really
forgotten? Hym;

05:01.002 --> 05:03.439
You swore a vow
to Lord Hadlar.

05:07.180 --> 05:09.753
After Fenbren's disobedience,

05:09.786 --> 05:13.492
how could we possibly
abandon our position now?

05:14.161 --> 05:15.998
Yes, you're right.

05:17.434 --> 05:20.474
I realize that our
purpose here is to allow

05:20.508 --> 05:24.750
Lord Hadlar to fight
Dai and Baran alone.

05:24.783 --> 05:25.685
W-What?!

05:25.718 --> 05:26.953
That means...

05:28.389 --> 05:31.362
We'll have to take
care of you ourselves.

05:35.872 --> 05:38.143
Popp [thought]: Hadlar
really thinks he can take on

05:38.176 --> 05:40.681
two Dragon Knights
at the same time?

05:49.766 --> 05:51.069
Hadlar?!

05:51.102 --> 05:53.139
And he's... alone.

05:55.009 --> 05:57.615
[pained roar]

06:10.207 --> 06:11.877
Albinass: Impossible.

06:11.910 --> 06:13.379
How can he even stand?!

06:13.412 --> 06:17.822
Perfect. I wouldn't
have this any other way.

06:19.358 --> 06:20.127
Popp: Hyunckel!

06:20.160 --> 06:21.863
Everyone - get up.

06:21.897 --> 06:25.938
We'll deal with them,
then go after Dai and Baran.

06:27.608 --> 06:29.846
Even after taking
all that damage...

06:29.879 --> 06:32.886
He still made his way
to the battlefield.

06:32.919 --> 06:36.560
Is he even actually
human? How can he be?

06:36.593 --> 06:39.131
No, I think he
must be immortal.

06:39.164 --> 06:41.803
Just like us.

06:43.874 --> 06:46.212
Maam [thought]:
Hyunckel, this is crazy.

06:46.246 --> 06:48.517
How did you even get here?

06:49.318 --> 06:51.088
Crocodine: [chuckling]

06:51.121 --> 06:53.392
Crocodine [thought]: That
magnificent, reckless fool.

06:53.426 --> 06:55.597
Crocodine: Hey,
you big brute...

06:57.267 --> 07:00.607
I've had just
about enough of you!

07:06.185 --> 07:07.722
[victorious chirping]

07:07.755 --> 07:10.460
But, Hyunckel...
are you sure about this?

07:10.493 --> 07:12.230
It won't be easy.

07:12.264 --> 07:13.901
Hyunckel: Don't
worry about me.

07:13.934 --> 07:15.103
He's right.

07:15.137 --> 07:18.210
What's worrying about the guy
gonna accomplish, anyway?

07:18.243 --> 07:19.411
Nothing!

07:19.444 --> 07:21.316
He's gonna do
whatever he wants!

07:21.349 --> 07:22.384
Hey - Popp!

07:22.417 --> 07:24.454
Popp: I'm glad
you're here, Hyunckel.

07:25.557 --> 07:29.632
Having you standing behind
us is more than enough.

07:29.666 --> 07:34.007
You're still our senior...
Disciple of Avan.

07:36.379 --> 07:37.849
He's right.

07:37.882 --> 07:41.155
Even if you can't
fight alongside us...

07:41.189 --> 07:43.894
You showing up is the
kind of courageous act

07:43.927 --> 07:47.067
that we need in
moments like this.

07:47.100 --> 07:48.637
We won't lose.

07:49.639 --> 07:52.244
You can sit this
one out, Hyunckel.

07:52.277 --> 07:54.247
I appreciate the concern...

07:54.281 --> 07:58.289
but standing by while you fight
may be even harder for me.

07:58.322 --> 07:59.859
Let's do this.

08:00.493 --> 08:02.163
Take a compliment.

08:05.671 --> 08:07.842
No more bishop...

08:07.875 --> 08:09.144
Is it dead?

08:09.178 --> 08:10.246
Probably.

08:10.280 --> 08:12.250
Dai and Baran must've won.

08:12.283 --> 08:13.653
Dai and Baran?

08:14.789 --> 08:17.427
It looks like they already
had our plan figured out.

08:17.460 --> 08:21.102
Hadlar's waiting
to take them both on.

08:21.135 --> 08:24.643
Hyunckel [thought]: He plans
to fight two Dragon Knights...

08:24.676 --> 08:26.478
Does he stand a chance?

08:26.513 --> 08:29.318
Or does he intend to die?

08:29.351 --> 08:32.626
Or... could it be both?

08:32.659 --> 08:34.261
We need to get moving.

08:34.294 --> 08:36.633
Let's not show them any mercy.

08:36.667 --> 08:39.839
Hym: That's supposed
to be our line.

08:39.872 --> 08:44.047
You aren't the only ones who
can't afford to lose this fight.

08:44.081 --> 08:47.955
Let's end this pointless
saga once and for all.

08:47.989 --> 08:52.097
So, let's see which of
us will get the honor!

08:56.372 --> 08:58.877
Hadlar: I don't
have much time.

08:59.779 --> 09:02.985
So why don't we begin, then?

09:03.019 --> 09:05.691
What kind of
game is this, Hadlar?

09:05.725 --> 09:08.430
Do you really think the
two of us are so weak...

09:08.463 --> 09:12.004
that you can win this
thing by yourself?

09:12.037 --> 09:12.905
[chuckling]

09:12.938 --> 09:14.041
Of course not.

09:14.074 --> 09:16.947
Dragon Knights are
the ultimate creations,

09:16.980 --> 09:21.055
a vision from
the gods, themselves.

09:21.088 --> 09:24.395
Knowing that one
was serving under me...

09:24.428 --> 09:26.733
It filled me with fear.

09:26.767 --> 09:31.208
Fear that someday you
would come after my throne.

09:31.241 --> 09:35.618
And when I learned Dai here
was also a Dragon Knight,

09:35.651 --> 09:38.088
I knew that day would come.

09:38.122 --> 09:42.899
I imagined the two of you
working together to defeat me.

09:42.932 --> 09:46.305
Now that fear has
become a reality.

09:46.339 --> 09:50.548
Nevertheless, I find myself
looking forward to this.

09:50.581 --> 09:53.720
Life can be
strange, can it not?

09:53.754 --> 09:57.127
Dai [thought]: He's been
planning to fight both of us

09:57.160 --> 09:58.664
from the start.

09:58.697 --> 10:02.706
Hadlar: Fenbren's
insubordination was unexpected.

10:02.739 --> 10:05.143
It seems that within me,

10:05.176 --> 10:08.015
there was still some
lingering narcissism

10:08.049 --> 10:11.488
and a desire for glory
in battle, after all.

10:11.523 --> 10:12.992
The Forbidden Magic I used

10:13.026 --> 10:16.966
imbued his personality
with both those things.

10:17.000 --> 10:21.709
Children tend to grow up to be
their parents, don't they?

10:23.112 --> 10:26.820
Now I shall defeat
Dai, the Hero!

10:26.854 --> 10:31.763
And Baran, if you should choose
to defend the boy in any way,

10:31.797 --> 10:34.802
I will destroy both
of you for good.

10:35.504 --> 10:36.573
Baran: You fool!

10:36.606 --> 10:39.946
Spare me your
arrogance, Hadlar.

10:39.979 --> 10:43.119
It seems that your power
has grown in some ways...

10:43.152 --> 10:45.992
But do not assume that you
have the strength to take on

10:46.025 --> 10:48.630
two Dragon Knights
at one time.

10:48.663 --> 10:52.771
The cost will be immensely
high, I can assure you.

11:13.346 --> 11:14.181
Dai: Wait!

11:14.214 --> 11:16.854
I don't think
Hadlar's being arrogant;

11:16.887 --> 11:19.425
He's transformed into
a Superior Being.

11:19.458 --> 11:21.062
A Superior Being?

11:21.095 --> 11:23.701
Dai: Yes. I think he
might be way more powerful

11:23.734 --> 11:25.905
than either one of us.

11:25.938 --> 11:28.042
That's why we have to
him fight together!

11:28.076 --> 11:31.048
It's the only sure way
that we can win this thing.

11:31.082 --> 11:31.883
Nonsense.

11:31.917 --> 11:33.887
Don't you know your
strength, boy?

11:33.920 --> 11:36.325
There's no need
to fight together.

11:36.358 --> 11:39.766
Have you no pride at all
in being a Dragon Knight?

11:39.799 --> 11:43.573
If I could win this with
just pride, I would.

11:43.606 --> 11:45.678
Dai: You already
said it yourself.

11:45.711 --> 11:48.884
Our real target is King Vearn.

11:48.917 --> 11:50.286
[frustrated growl]

11:52.859 --> 11:54.896
Vearn: And so it begins.

11:54.929 --> 11:59.338
The great climactic battle
we've all been waiting for.

11:59.371 --> 12:02.243
Who will gain the upper hand?

12:02.277 --> 12:05.618
Mystvearn: Hadlar may
have become quite powerful,

12:05.651 --> 12:11.563
but against the full fury of
Dai and Baran, he cannot win.

12:11.597 --> 12:14.502
Isolating himself
from his Royal Guard

12:14.535 --> 12:17.140
was an act of pure madness.

12:17.173 --> 12:18.710
Madness, you say?

12:18.744 --> 12:21.214
No. He's desperate.

12:21.248 --> 12:23.118
He's backed himself
into a corner

12:23.152 --> 12:25.323
to push his
strength even further.

12:25.356 --> 12:26.626
Don't you see?

12:26.660 --> 12:29.699
Quite a clever ploy
for our Hadlar.

12:29.732 --> 12:31.301
Mystvearn: But,
should he be defeated,

12:31.335 --> 12:36.513
the Dragons will gain entrance
to the citadel, will they not?

12:36.547 --> 12:38.416
Vearn: That won't happen.

12:38.449 --> 12:39.618
Mystvearn: No?

12:39.652 --> 12:44.028
I believe they will find it
quite impossible, Mystvearn.

12:44.061 --> 12:48.803
The father and son
will never see my face.

12:50.775 --> 12:52.978
I was mistaken, Dai.

12:53.012 --> 12:55.918
I was sure that you had
grown as a warrior...

12:55.952 --> 12:58.590
But it seems to me that
you're still far from

12:58.623 --> 13:00.827
becoming a true Dragon Knight.

13:00.861 --> 13:02.932
You're mistaking
arrogance for pride.

13:02.965 --> 13:05.002
There's more important
things at stake.

13:05.035 --> 13:08.475
I don't need to be a "true
Dragon Knight" to see that.

13:08.510 --> 13:10.681
Besides, I'm part human...

13:10.715 --> 13:12.985
I'll never be
the same as you.

13:16.057 --> 13:17.929
I'm fighting
for all my friends.

13:17.962 --> 13:20.735
And I'm going to do
the very best I can-

13:20.768 --> 13:22.437
the best I'm capable of.

13:22.470 --> 13:27.013
For me, defeating Vearn and
Hadlar means saving the world.

13:27.047 --> 13:29.919
My pride isn't going
to get in the way.

13:30.588 --> 13:32.223
Dai...

13:32.257 --> 13:35.831
Hadlar: Enough talk.
Who will fight?

13:35.864 --> 13:39.605
Or are both of you too afraid?

13:42.143 --> 13:44.949
Let's settle this,
Hadlar! Just us!

13:44.982 --> 13:47.622
If you're not gonna
listen to reason, Baran,

13:47.655 --> 13:50.059
I don't have a choice.

13:50.092 --> 13:53.065
You'll see in just
a few seconds.

13:53.667 --> 13:56.405
So the boy dies first.

13:56.439 --> 13:58.008
We'll see!

14:00.179 --> 14:02.016
Hadlar has a hidden sword?!

14:02.719 --> 14:04.320
[roaring]

14:09.733 --> 14:11.869
[roaring]

14:13.840 --> 14:15.443
Hadlar: [laughing]

14:15.477 --> 14:16.680
Good, Dai!

14:16.713 --> 14:21.455
You've truly improved since the
last time we crossed blades.

14:31.041 --> 14:32.945
Baran [thought]: Dai
was right about him...

14:32.978 --> 14:36.418
The power of the attacks
he's unleashing rivals my own.

14:37.655 --> 14:39.324
Hadlar: How very generous.

14:40.359 --> 14:43.165
Hadlar: To fight in
place of your father,

14:43.198 --> 14:46.539
who has no
experience against me.

14:46.573 --> 14:47.976
However...

14:48.009 --> 14:50.881
it's not as though
you know the full extent

14:50.915 --> 14:54.154
of my powers either, boy.

14:57.326 --> 14:59.264
What kind of weapon is that?!

14:59.297 --> 15:01.067
Hell's Chain!

15:04.976 --> 15:06.478
[pained cry]

15:07.748 --> 15:09.284
Boom!

15:25.584 --> 15:27.655
Avan... Strash!

15:27.688 --> 15:29.592
Kaboom!

15:36.405 --> 15:37.373
Dai!

15:39.579 --> 15:43.452
Dai... Are you all right?

15:43.485 --> 15:46.291
[pained groaning]

15:46.325 --> 15:47.595
[chuckle]

15:47.628 --> 15:49.598
Wh-what did I tell you?

15:50.499 --> 15:52.470
Baran: I see now.

15:52.504 --> 15:57.346
Hadlar's power is great.
He's a menace.

16:00.754 --> 16:03.159
Well, well. Dai.

16:03.192 --> 16:07.735
Even after all this time.
You still surprise me.

16:07.768 --> 16:09.137
You and me both.

16:09.170 --> 16:13.546
He completely negated my
Strash with his Kaboom spell.

16:13.580 --> 16:16.719
A wound like that will
regenerate in no time.

16:20.561 --> 16:21.996
It can't be!

16:22.397 --> 16:24.067
No... it is!

16:24.100 --> 16:25.771
The infernal coal.

16:25.804 --> 16:27.608
A Black Core!

16:27.641 --> 16:29.044
What's a "black core"?

16:29.077 --> 16:30.814
Baran [thought]:
How could the Dark King

16:30.848 --> 16:33.285
do something so barbaric?

16:33.319 --> 16:37.326
To implant such a device
in his own servant...

16:38.697 --> 16:40.433
Mystvearn: A Black Core?!

16:40.466 --> 16:44.942
And you hid this in
the body you gave Hadlar?

16:44.975 --> 16:47.347
Vearn: Now do you understand?

16:47.380 --> 16:51.455
I told you those two
will never see my face.

16:51.488 --> 16:54.460
If they manage
to defeat Hadlar,

16:54.494 --> 16:58.302
they will detonate the Black
Core hidden in his body,

16:58.336 --> 17:03.379
creating a destructive blast.
At the very least...

17:03.412 --> 17:07.086
We can bring this
battle to a draw.

17:07.654 --> 17:08.656
Mystvearn: A draw?

17:08.690 --> 17:13.232
It will blow away the
entire Field of Death.

17:13.266 --> 17:16.138
Vearn: Perhaps,
but no matter.

17:16.171 --> 17:19.612
No harm will
befall my palace.

17:20.814 --> 17:22.250
After all,

17:22.284 --> 17:26.626
their battle is taking
place out on the perimeter.

17:30.299 --> 17:32.705
That thing's... a bomb?

17:32.739 --> 17:33.940
Baran: That's right.

17:33.973 --> 17:38.048
A super-powered one from the
Underworld called a Black Core.

17:38.082 --> 17:39.719
It's a nightmarish weapon-

17:39.752 --> 17:43.526
one even more devastating
than you can imagine.

17:43.560 --> 17:46.264
But... How do
you know about that?

17:46.298 --> 17:49.671
I've seen it before.
When I was in the Underworld.

17:49.705 --> 17:54.047
Black Cores are made from
a stone called Black Crystal.

17:54.080 --> 17:55.951
It's found deep
in the Underworld

17:55.985 --> 17:58.790
and absorbs power
from the very earth.

17:58.823 --> 18:02.063
They're weaponized
using Old Magic.

18:02.096 --> 18:05.302
However, due to their
extreme destructive power,

18:05.335 --> 18:08.342
even evil creatures who have
dedicated their existence

18:08.376 --> 18:13.252
to Forbidden Magic fear
using these Black Cores.

18:13.286 --> 18:14.888
Thirteen years ago,

18:14.922 --> 18:18.864
when Hadlar was Dark Lord and
ravaged the surface world,

18:18.897 --> 18:24.440
I fought Velzar, King of
the Abyss, in the Underworld.

18:25.476 --> 18:28.650
During that battle in
the depths of the earth,

18:28.683 --> 18:32.758
Velzar used a
Black Core against me.

18:32.792 --> 18:34.061
Dai: What happened?

18:34.094 --> 18:38.168
Baran: His entire
region was vaporized.

18:39.806 --> 18:45.382
In his attempt to vanquish me,
he destroyed his own kingdom.

18:46.051 --> 18:49.224
After that, even Velzar...

18:49.258 --> 18:52.999
He refused to use
a Black Core again.

18:53.032 --> 18:54.602
His great ambition...

18:54.636 --> 18:59.578
Was to rule the Underworld and
conquer the surface continents.

18:59.612 --> 19:03.686
He wasn't going to risk
destroying them both.

19:03.720 --> 19:06.124
Baran [thought]: But for
Vearn to resort to using

19:06.157 --> 19:07.795
a Black Core...

19:07.828 --> 19:12.170
It seems his plan is not
to rule the surface world,

19:12.203 --> 19:15.510
but to annihilate
it completely.

19:18.883 --> 19:23.459
Vearn: I never intended for
Hadlar to be a sacrificial pawn.

19:23.492 --> 19:26.666
But when I saved him
from the brink of death,

19:26.699 --> 19:30.541
I implanted the
Black Core as insurance.

19:30.574 --> 19:36.352
Then he went and transformed
himself into a Superior Being.

19:36.385 --> 19:40.460
This was something
even I did not expect.

19:40.493 --> 19:44.334
The increase in his power
has had an adverse effect

19:44.367 --> 19:46.338
on the Black Core.

19:46.371 --> 19:49.044
It is no longer stable.

19:49.077 --> 19:53.385
The bomb could be
set off at any moment.

19:54.521 --> 19:58.228
I believe that this will
manifest itself in Hadlar

19:58.262 --> 20:00.900
with bouts of
excruciating agony.

20:00.934 --> 20:04.273
Of course, he'll likely
assume that the pain is

20:04.307 --> 20:08.716
a product of the little
experiment done to his body.

20:08.750 --> 20:13.225
Knowing the outcome of a
battle is a boring thing...

20:13.258 --> 20:16.131
A horrible shame.

20:16.164 --> 20:20.907
But even still,
we must see it through.

20:20.940 --> 20:23.513
He has been a valuable servant,

20:23.546 --> 20:26.185
but this may be
the final performance

20:26.218 --> 20:28.790
of our dear old Hadlar.

20:31.127 --> 20:32.430
Mystvearn [thought]: Tragic...

20:32.463 --> 20:36.037
Finally finding
the warrior inside him

20:36.071 --> 20:39.845
has ultimately
shortened his life.

20:39.878 --> 20:42.250
Ironic, even.

20:42.283 --> 20:46.626
While I would prefer that
he win and survive...

20:46.659 --> 20:52.103
Should he fall, at least he'll
go out in a blaze of glory.

20:52.137 --> 20:54.174
If only he knew
that his demise

20:54.207 --> 20:57.514
could bring our
Dark king victory.

21:00.854 --> 21:04.093
If the Black Core explodes,
we'll be in trouble.

21:04.126 --> 21:05.897
What do we do?

21:05.930 --> 21:07.167
I don't know.

21:07.200 --> 21:08.569
Dai: What?!

21:08.603 --> 21:12.511
And Dai, we can't use any spells
or swords in this battle.

21:12.544 --> 21:14.716
Fight only with blunt force.

21:14.749 --> 21:18.155
Hang on - seriously?
But we'll never win!

21:18.189 --> 21:20.392
Baran: Just listen to me!

21:20.426 --> 21:22.363
That Black Core
has been imbued with

21:22.397 --> 21:24.768
a terrifying amount
of Magic Power.

21:24.802 --> 21:27.340
It must be completely
filled after absorbing

21:27.373 --> 21:30.947
some of Hadlar's
transformed energy, as well.

21:30.980 --> 21:34.354
Simply hitting it with a
powerful spell of any kind

21:34.387 --> 21:36.491
might set it off.

21:37.994 --> 21:39.899
Hadlar: Are you done planning?

21:39.932 --> 21:42.103
I'll take you both on!

21:42.136 --> 21:44.340
Now, ready or not.

21:49.652 --> 21:53.359
[roaring]

21:53.392 --> 21:55.162
Hadlar! Is... he-

21:55.196 --> 21:57.499
Oh, no. He's coming!

23:38.803 --> 23:40.773
Narrator: To avoid
setting off the Black Core

23:40.807 --> 23:42.978
and alerting Hadlar
of its presence,

23:43.011 --> 23:45.751
Dai and Baran must hold
back their attacks.

23:45.784 --> 23:48.088
But the Dark Lord hounds
them relentlessly,

23:48.121 --> 23:51.629
and when he prepares to unleash
his Ultra Combustion Slash,

23:51.662 --> 23:54.301
Baran confronts the
overwhelming onslaught

23:54.334 --> 23:56.572
with a gambit of his own...

23:56.605 --> 23:58.475
See how it unfolds
next time on

23:58.509 --> 24:01.381
Dragon Quest:
The Adventure of Dai,

24:01.414 --> 24:03.786
"Hadlar Versus Baran".
